refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
intfalsesocket_send Socketsocket stringdata intlength intflags
The function socket_send sends at most length bytes to the socket socket from data.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
socket_send returns the number of bytes sent, or &false; on error. The number of bytes sent can be lower than length, for example on a non-blocking socket, with MSG_DONTWAIT, with a send timeout or after a signal: a loop must be used to send the rest of data.
When nothing can be sent, &false; is returned, without any warning for SOCKET_EAGAIN and with an E_WARNING for the other errors. The error code can be retrieved with socket_last_error and passed to socket_strerror to get a textual explanation.

